## Goal

Stinkyscape+ #94 PIP's faces say "performance **improvement** plan" (was "performance **enhancement** plan") in the spec (§8.12 row 94), `catalog.json`, the script header, the engine fixture comment and the designer source, with nothing else about the card changed. A pending micro fragment (`tier:micro`, `kind:cards`) claims the wording change with a hand-written player note, and `classify --claims` finds no card playing differently (no `--plays`, no `KEPT_SCRIPTS` entry). New ruling R4996000 (note plus `spec/pending/4996.md` paragraph) locks the exact term on every face in every locale the client shows, proved by a test named after it.

## Files to touch

| File | New/change | What changes |
|---|---|---|
| `spec/08-catalog/8.12-stinkyscape-plus.md` | change | Row 170: `enhancement` → `improvement` in both face-text cells; one `[[R4996000]]` sentence appended to the description cell |
| `crates/cards/catalog.json` | change | `stinkyscapeplus-094` base and radiant `text`: same word swap; `params`, `loc`, keywords untouched |
| `crates/cards/src/scripts/stinkyscape_plus/c094_pip.rs` | change | Header line 2 quoted base text: same word swap only; `pip()`, `script()`, `mod tests` untouched |
| `crates/engine/tests/rules/fixtures/combat_reactions.rs` | change | Line 51 `PIP` doc comment: same word swap |
| `JackiOh_StinkyscapePlus_Cards.md` | change | Lines 1003, 1005: same word swap; bold markup and trailing spaces kept |
| `crates/cards/patches/pending/pip-says-performance-improvement-plan.json` | new | Fragment written by the `patches` command, plus hand-written `player` note under `text` |
| `spec/rulings/R4996000.md` | new | Ruling note: front matter and body |
| `spec/pending/4996.md` | new | One §11 paragraph for R4996000 |
| `crates/tools/tests/export_card_text.rs` | change | Add `fn r4996000_pip_names_the_plan_in_every_locale` |

Do not touch: `crates/cards/patches/v*.json`, `patches.json`, `shipped.json`, `index.json`, `records/`, `crates/cards/card-text.yaml` (the `zh` faces already read 绩效改进计划), `crates/cards/chinese.json`, `flavour.json`, `apps/web/src/audio/voice-text.json`, `spec/history/`, `spec/INDEX.md`, `spec/CARDS.md`, anything under `.github/`, `.harness/`, `.squishy/`, `bot/`. Never run `cargo jackioh spec index` (a daily job owns it). Governing: SPEC §8.12; R3550006/R3557006 (cited, unchanged); `docs/ADDING_CARDS.md` §3; `docs/issues-and-patches.md` (fragment and player-note numbers); CLAUDE.md rules 3, 5, 6. No number changes, so rule 9 is uninvolved (`count`, `count2`, `the` stay as they are).

## Steps

Before each edit below, `grep -n` the find string and confirm it matches exactly as stated. Change only the word `enhancement` → `improvement` in each quoted text; touch no other word (the header's "they have {count} turn" phrasing stays).

1. `spec/08-catalog/8.12-stinkyscape-plus.md`, row 170. One edit whose find spans both face cells: find `performance enhancement plan, they have 1 turn to get a kill otherwise they are destroyed | Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan` (matches once: the `|` is the cell boundary between the base and Radiant faces), replace with the same string with both occurrences as `performance improvement plan`. Then append the ruling link to the description cell: find `the 3 ↑ (the Radiant face's). Built by S18 (#3557). |`, replace with `the 3 ↑ (the Radiant face's). Built by S18 (#3557). Both faces name the plan ([[R4996000]]). |`.
2. `crates/cards/catalog.json`. Two edits: find `"text": "Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan: it has {count|turn|turns} to get a kill, or it is destroyed."` → `improvement` version (matches once); find `"text": "Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan: it has {count2|turn|turns} to get a kill, or it is destroyed. If it fails, add {the|The Coin|The Coins} to your hand."` → `improvement` version (matches once).
3. `crates/cards/src/scripts/stinkyscape_plus/c094_pip.rs`, line 2. Find `//!   Base:    "Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan, they have {count} turn to get a kill` → `improvement` (matches once). Leave `pip()`, `script()`, `ID`, `mod tests` alone.
4. `crates/engine/tests/rules/fixtures/combat_reactions.rs`, line 51. Find `/// A Spell: "Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan..." (PIP's shape).` → `improvement` (matches once).
5. `JackiOh_StinkyscapePlus_Cards.md`. Line 1003: find `Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan, they have 1 turn to get a kill otherwise they are destroyed.  ` (two trailing spaces) → `improvement`, keeping the spaces. Line 1005: find `Put a Unit on a performance enhancement plan, they have 1 turn to get a kill otherwise they are destroyed. If they fail, add 3 **The Coins** to your hand.` → `improvement`, keeping the bold markup.
6. Claim the patch. Run `cargo jackioh patches "PIP says performance improvement plan" --source "#4996" --notes "Stinkyscape+ #94 PIP's text reads 'performance improvement plan' (was 'performance enhancement plan')."` It writes `crates/cards/patches/pending/pip-says-performance-improvement-plan.json` (slug is the title lower-cased and dashed). Open that file, change nothing the command wrote, and fill in the `player` note by hand as `{"title": "PIP says performance improvement plan", "text": ["PIP: now says \"performance improvement plan\"."]}` with `new`, `balance`, `changes`, `fixes` left as the command left them (empty). The line names no ruling, issue, card number or `§`, per the player-note rules.
7. Write `spec/rulings/R4996000.md` with this front matter and body:
```markdown
---
id: R4996000
title: "PIP names the plan word for word (issue #4996)"
cards: "§8.12, S+ #94 PIP (issue #4996)"
proven_in:
  - crates/tools/tests/export_card_text.rs
---
PIP names the plan word for word. Every face of Stinkyscape+ #94 PIP (base and Radiant) contains the exact phrase "performance improvement plan" in English, and in every other language the client shows (`card-text.yaml`'s locales: Simplified Chinese, `zh`, today) that language's standard term for one. In Simplified Chinese that is 绩效改进计划. No face says it any other way, such as "performance enhancement plan", "performance plan" or "PEP". A language added later must name the plan by its own standard term, and this ruling's test covers it from the day it lands. It edits [[§8.12]]'s S+ #94 row, the faces' words alone.

Hearthstone semantics: no Hearthstone rule names the plan; the English words are fixed as above.
```
8. Write `spec/pending/4996.md` (new file) holding one paragraph: `**[[R4996000]] PIP names the plan word for word (issue #4996, <today's date in YYYY-MM-DD>)**: issue #4996 fixes Stinkyscape+ #94 PIP's faces, which told players a Unit is put on a "performance enhancement plan": both faces now read "performance improvement plan". It edits [[§8.12]]'s S+ #94 row, the faces' words alone, and takes R4996000, the first number of issue #4996's block.`
9. Add the proving test at the end of `crates/tools/tests/export_card_text.rs` (it already imports `jackioh_cards::CATALOG` and reads `card-text.yaml` through `yaml_serde`; this file is chosen because it is the only test that sees every locale key — pure crates cannot parse YAML per rule 4, so `cross/chinese.rs` and the card's own `mod tests` can only see locales with compiled-in sidecars; precedent: R1303's `proven_in` already lists this file):
```rust
#[test]
fn r4996000_pip_names_the_plan_in_every_locale() {
    // R4996000: S+ #94 PIP names a performance improvement plan on every face,
    // in English and in every locale card-text.yaml shows (`zh` today).
    const ID: &str = "stinkyscapeplus-094";
    const TERMS: &[(&str, &str)] = &[
        ("en", "performance improvement plan"),
        ("zh", "绩效改进计划"),
    ];
    const NOT_WORDS: &[&str] = &["enhancement", "PEP", "performance plan"];
    const META: &[&str] = &["flavour", "artist", "voice"];
    let term = |locale: &str| {
        TERMS
            .iter()
            .find(|(code, _)| *code == locale)
            .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("R4996000: no term for locale {locale:?}: add its row to TERMS"))
            .1
    };
    let card = &CATALOG[ID];
    for face in [&card.base.text, &card.radiant.text] {
        assert!(face.contains(term("en")), "R4996000: {face:?} lacks the plan's name");
        for other in NOT_WORDS {
            assert!(!face.contains(other), "R4996000: {face:?} says it as {other:?}");
        }
    }
    let text = std::fs::read_to_string(YAML).unwrap_or_else(|error| panic!("{YAML}: {error}"));
    let root: yaml_serde::Mapping =
        yaml_serde::from_str(&text).unwrap_or_else(|error| panic!("card-text.yaml: {error}"));
    let entry = root
        .get(&yaml_serde::Value::String(ID.to_string()))
        .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("card-text.yaml: no {ID} entry"));
    let entry = entry.as_mapping().unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("card-text.yaml: {ID} is not a mapping"));
    let mut seen: Vec<&str> = vec!["en"];
    for (key, value) in entry {
        let Some(field) = key.as_str() else { continue };
        if META.contains(&field) {
            continue;
        }
        let faces = value
            .as_mapping()
            .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("card-text.yaml: {ID}.{field} is not a locale"));
        let get = |face: &str| {
            faces
                .get(&yaml_serde::Value::String(face.to_string()))
                .and_then(|v| v.as_str())
                .unwrap_or_else(|| panic!("card-text.yaml: {ID}.{field} has no {face}"))
        };
        for face in [get("base"), get("radiant")] {
            assert!(face.contains(term(field)), "R4996000: {ID}.{field} lacks its term");
        }
        seen.push(field);
    }
    let mut want: Vec<&str> = TERMS.iter().map(|(code, _)| *code).collect();
    seen.sort_unstable();
    want.sort_unstable();
    assert_eq!(seen, want, "R4996000: locales shown and locales in TERMS differ");
}
```
A locale added to `card-text.yaml` later reaches the loop as a non-`META` mapping and fails on the missing `TERMS` row instead of passing silently; a removed locale fails the final equality.
10. Prove the test locks the wording (temporary flips, each restored immediately, running only the new test between): `sed -i 's/performance improvement plan: it has/performance enhancement plan: it has/' crates/cards/catalog.json`, then `cargo test -p jackioh-tools --test export_card_text r4996000` must FAIL; restore with `sed -i 's/performance enhancement plan: it has/performance improvement plan: it has/' crates/cards/catalog.json`, test must PASS. Then `sed -i 's/绩效改进计划/绩效增强计划/' crates/cards/card-text.yaml` (confirm beforehand it hits exactly the 2 PIP lines), test must FAIL; restore with the reverse `sed`, test must PASS. If any restore leaves the tree wrong, the greps and suite in step 11 catch it.

## Tests

- `crates/tools/tests/export_card_text.rs`, `r4996000_pip_names_the_plan_in_every_locale`: asserts both CATALOG English faces contain `performance improvement plan` and none of `enhancement`/`PEP`/contiguous `performance plan`; both `zh` faces from `card-text.yaml` contain 绩效改进计划; every locale key on PIP's YAML entry has a `TERMS` row and vice versa. Run `cargo test -p jackioh-tools --test export_card_text` (also runs the export-staleness check, which must rewrite nothing, and the existing `r660_r1303_…` test).
- `crates/cards/src/scripts/stinkyscape_plus/c094_pip.rs`, existing `mod tests` (`a_unit_that_gets_a_kill_in_time_lives`, `a_unit_without_a_kill_is_destroyed_and_the_base_face_adds_no_coin`, `radiant_adds_three_coins_when_it_fails`, `r3557006_…`): rules unchanged, must stay green. Run `cargo test -p jackioh-cards c094_pip`.
- `crates/cards/tests/cross/` (unchanged files, guards the catalog edit): run `cargo test -p jackioh-cards --test cross`.
- Checks: `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo clippy -p jackioh-cards --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cargo clippy -p jackioh-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cargo clippy -p jackioh-engine --all-targets -- -D warnings`; `cargo jackioh catalog check`; `cargo jackioh patches check`; `cargo jackioh spec check`; `cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims` (expect micro/cards wording only, no plays). No web, e2e or database tests: no files under `apps/`, `e2e/` or `crates/server/` change.
- Greps: `git grep -n "performance enhancement"` must list only `crates/cards/patches/v*.json` lines; `git grep -n "performance improvement plan"` must list the spec row, both catalog texts, the script header, the fixture comment and both designer lines.

## Done when

- [ ] Both PIP faces read "performance improvement plan" in the §8.12 row, `catalog.json`, the script header, the fixture comment and the designer source; `git grep -n "performance enhancement"` finds nothing outside `crates/cards/patches/v*.json`.
- [ ] `spec/rulings/R4996000.md` and `spec/pending/4996.md` exist and `cargo jackioh spec check` passes.
- [ ] `r4996000_pip_names_the_plan_in_every_locale` passes, and was seen to fail on the flipped English text and on the flipped `zh` face.
- [ ] `cargo jackioh catalog check`, `cargo jackioh patches check` and `cargo jackioh classify --base origin/main --claims` pass, the last with no card playing differently (no `--plays`).
- [ ] `cargo test -p jackioh-cards c094_pip`, `cargo test -p jackioh-cards --test cross` and `cargo test -p jackioh-tools --test export_card_text` pass; `cargo fmt --check` and the three `clippy -p` runs are clean; no generated sidecar was rewritten.

## Risks

- `classify` unexpectedly naming playing cards: the script and params are untouched, so this should not happen; if it does, stop and report rather than adding `--plays` blindly.
- `export_card_text` rewriting `chinese.json`, `flavour.json` or `voice-text.json`: `card-text.yaml` is untouched, so it should rewrite nothing; a rewrite means an unrelated YAML drift — stop and report.
- The temporary-flip seds in step 10 must be restored exactly; the closing greps and test runs verify the restore.
- The `[[R4996000]]` sentence added to the §8.12 row sits in the rules-description cell, not a face-text cell, so REVIEW Part A (spec versus designer source) still compares identical face texts.

## Open questions

None. No step needs a person, a secret, a dashboard or a forbidden path; difficulty stays medium (a wording change plus one ruling and its tests, no engine rules, no AI, no migration, nine files).

